.env.local
node_modules/
dist/
# The SSR bundle the prerender step builds and imports. Build output like
# `dist`, and never published: it is deliberately kept OUT of `dist`, which is
# collected wholesale and shipped to R2.
dist-ssr/
.DS_Store
shots/

# Scratch log written by scripts/build-as-owner.mjs on a local run
build-as-owner-log.md

# The two repair workflows end their command in `| tee <name>.log`, so running a
# step's real `run:` text by hand — which is how the argument-injection defect
# was reproduced — drops the log in the repository root. One was committed that
# way. The workflow itself is unaffected: it writes this file in the runner's
# workspace and uploads it as an artifact; it never commits.
backend-repair.log
repairbench-count-fix.log
